Welcome to the Cisco Umbrella kit. This kit is designed to help you understand, query, and make the most of the logs generated by Cisco Umbrella.

This playbook serves to get you oriented around the kit and provide some anchors into the data and dashboards.

# Getting Data In

Cisco Umbrella exports logs as gzip-compressed CSV files to an Amazon S3 bucket, either a Cisco-managed bucket or a self-managed bucket in your own AWS account. Configure log export in the Umbrella dashboard under **Admin > Log Management**, then use the Gravwell Kinesis/S3 ingest options (or the File Follower against synced files) to bring the logs in. Assign each log source to its own tag:

| Log source | S3 subfolder | Tag |
|---|---|---|
| DNS logs | `dnslogs` | `umbrella-dns` |
| Proxy logs | `proxylogs` | `umbrella-proxy` |
| Admin audit logs | `auditlogs` | `umbrella-audit` |

Log format references from Cisco:

- [DNS Log Formats](https://securitydocs.cisco.com/docs/umbrella-dns/olh/147415.dita)
- [Proxy Log Formats](https://securitydocs.cisco.com/docs/umbrella-dns/olh/147416.dita)
- [Admin Audit Log Formats](https://securitydocs.cisco.com/docs/umbrella-dns/olh/147414.dita)

**Note:** Leave the optional log header row **disabled** in Umbrella. If enabled, each header line is ingested as an entry and the CSV extractors will parse it into fields whose values are the column names, adding spurious series such as `action`, `response_code`, and `categories` to the dashboard charts. The detections are unaffected, but the stats queries have no header guard.

# Overview

Umbrella logs for this kit come from 3 distinct sources.

## DNS Logs
Traffic that has reached the Umbrella DNS resolvers. Each entry records the requesting identity, internal and external IPs, the domain, query type, response code, the policy action taken (Allowed, Blocked, or Proxied), and the security/content categories of the destination. This kit ships autoextractors for the v13 DNS log schema.

## Proxy Logs
Traffic that has passed through the Umbrella intelligent proxy, including URL, HTTP method and status, file inspection results from the antivirus engine and Cisco AMP, DLP status, and certificate errors. This kit ships autoextractors for the v12 proxy log schema.

## Admin Audit Logs
Changes made by your administrative team in the Umbrella dashboard: who changed what, from which IP, with before and after values.

# Field Extraction

Umbrella logs are CSV with no embedded field names, so this kit ships an autoextractor for each tag. Queries reference fields through the `ax` module, for example:

```
tag=$UMBRELLA_DNS ax action=="Blocked" domain
| count by domain
| chart count by domain limit 10
```

If Cisco adds fields in a future schema version they will appear as additional columns; the extractors list every documented column and ignore any that are absent.

# Queries
Queries are broken out into 2 types and have appropriate labels applied for reference.

## Stats
Primarily used by dashboards to generate metrics and provide an overview of activity within the Umbrella environment.

## Detections
Queries built to detect specific behavior that can be indicative of malicious activity: requests to Command and Control, DNS tunneling, and cryptomining domains, allowed requests to malicious destinations, DGA-style NXDOMAIN bursts, AMP and antivirus file detections, DLP blocks, log export tampering, and suspicious administrator behavior. These can be used ad hoc, serve as a basis for your own detection engineering, or enabled as scheduled searches for alerting. Threshold-based detections should be tuned to your environment.

# Scheduled Searches
Every detection ships with a matching scheduled search that runs hourly over the previous two hours of data. The overlapping window accounts for Umbrella's batched S3 log delivery, so a threshold detection may alert twice for the same burst. They are **disabled by default** - review the thresholds, then enable the ones you want from the Scheduled Searches page.

# Dashboards
3 dashboards are provided in this kit.

## Umbrella - DNS Overview
High-level view of DNS activity. Request volume over time by action, blocked request trends, top blocked domains, query types, response codes, top identities, and top categories. Useful as the landing page.

## Umbrella - Web Proxy Overview
Traffic through the intelligent proxy: volume by action, bandwidth, top blocked categories, HTTP status codes, top destinations, and AMP malware detections.

## Umbrella - Administrative Audit
Administrative changes to the Umbrella configuration: change volume, changes by administrator, actions by type, recent changes, and log export configuration changes.

# Actionables
## Umbrella - Investigate Domain
When a domain appears in search results, an option under the "Umbrella" menu will run the domain investigation template against Umbrella DNS logs.

## Umbrella - Investigate Internal IP
When an IP address appears in search results, an option under the "Umbrella" menu will run the internal IP investigation template against Umbrella DNS logs.

# Templates
- **Umbrella - Investigate Domain** - DNS activity for a domain
- **Umbrella - Investigate Internal IP** - DNS activity from an internal host
- **Umbrella - Investigate Identity** - DNS activity for an Umbrella identity
- **Umbrella - Investigate Proxied URL** - proxy activity for a URL or hostname

# Macros
Three configuration macros control which tags the kit queries. If your tags differ from the defaults you must update **both** the macro value **and** the `Tag` on the matching autoextractor (Extractors page) - these logs are headerless CSV, so if the autoextractor is not bound to your tag, no fields will be extracted and every query in the kit will return empty results.

- `$UMBRELLA_DNS` (default `umbrella-dns`)
- `$UMBRELLA_PROXY` (default `umbrella-proxy`)
- `$UMBRELLA_AUDIT` (default `umbrella-audit`)
